About the Author
Dr. Linda Seger began her script consulting business in 1981, 也 a
script analysis method she developed as part of her doctoral dissertation
“What Makeさ Script Work?” Since then, she has consulted with writers,
producers, directors, and production companies on 包 2,000 scripts
and 100 produced filmさnd taught scriptwriting in thirty-one countries.
Among her many clients have been Ray Bradbury, Peter Jackson, William
Kelley, Tony Bill, ITC Entertainment, Charles Fries Entertainment, TriStar
Pictures, で Institute. She has given seminars for executives
at ABC, CBS, NBC, Disney, Embassy Television, RAI ã (Italy),
and ZDF ã ă, コ for members ¨ American
Film Institute, the Directors Guild of America, the Writers Guild of
America, the 店 Television Artさnd Sciences, ć Academy
of Motion Picture Artさnd Sciences. She î recipient of ź awards,
including the Living Legacy Award わ Moondance International Film
Festival. She î author of eight books on screenwriting. Her website is
